{
  "summary": "This experiment tested replacing the ResNet50 image encoder with ViT-L in a high-performing multiprofile configuration (scvi_n200 RNA, avgpool aggregation, weighted fusion), achieving higher validation accuracy (0.7062) and F1 (0.6671) compared to the previous ResNet50-based setup (0.6776). The result suggests ViT-L may improve performance in this context, though the role of other factors like fusion or aggregation remains untested. The impact of ViT-L's complexity on multiprofile scenarios requires further validation against alternative encoders."
}

